            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Joann Palmer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this because I remember my grandmother always having it at picnics. I took it to a pot luck and it was a rave !! I did substitute 1/2 of the mayo with greek plain yogurt."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nhbabs"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I found that making it per recipe it comes out quite bland for my tastebuds. However, I rated it 4 stars because it's a great combo that can easily be tweaked to greatness. I added 6 TBS of vinegar and 6 pks of nutrisweet, plus LOTs of salt and pepper. ( I added it 2TBS of vinegar at a time and kept tasting it until it tasted the way I thought was good) The basic recipe does have a hint of the sweet and sour, but it's very faint. I think using the greek yogurt with it's tanginess would help. I suggest making it with 1/2 yogurt and otherwise per recipe, then just tweek it until it has the taste you like. Certainly a healthy dish. Thank you for sharing it.",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-18T13:57:38.720Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Naleek"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make similar but no vinegar no sugar or peppers. Add 1/4 c sweet relish.. celery and onion. It is sooo good :)",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-23T03:11:40.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this a couple of times a month! We love it - I only use 1 tbsp of milk and use 1 tbsp apple cider vinegar and 1 tbsp white vinegar. I also omit the peppers and egg. Make sure beans are drained well or it will be watery. Thank you for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-21T01:15:27.257Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "5.5.20 I added the 1 cup mayonnaise to the bowl, and then saw that the recipe called for another 1/4 cup of liquid (milk and vinegar) and had concerns that this would turn out too runny. I cut it back some, and I’m glad I did because it still was pretty wet. I reduced the number of hard boiled eggs simply because they’re hard to find during this COVID-19 phase, and if you are lucky enough to find eggs, they’re outrageously expensive. I’ve made kidney bean salad many, many times, and this one measured up pretty well. I gave it a good grind of freshly-ground black pepper, and it was a nice side dish to some salmon patties.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-05T18:19:58.797Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jodi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy, yummy with lots of protein and potassium! Best the next day after sitting in refrigerator over night. I added half a cup of plain greek yogurt and of course a tiny bit more sugar :) 32oz of kidney beans is actually two cans. Great for summer.",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-09T05:21:25.993Z"
          },
